  "summary": "Held throughout: this long entry ran essentially straight from 0 to a +71.75pt peak with only shallow, short-lived dips (worst single-frame excursion was -8.75pts early on, and one deeper -3.25pt pullback around t=11m after a strong run-up), and it kept making new highs through t=45m before drifting sideways in the +45 to +70 range through the end of the window -- never once threatening the entry price or showing a sustained lower-high/lower-low breakdown. Nothing in the price action or the fire signatures (occasional KMDR/CLIMAX/PROPP-against readings near the highs looked like normal profit-taking chop, not a directional reversal) ever suggested the entry thesis was wrong; it was a clean, strongly-trending winner. Next time I'd watch for a confirmed break below a rising leg's prior swing low (not just giveback% off a local high) as the real wrong-direction tell, since giveback% alone was noisy on small legs."
